{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778601579879,"sessionID":"ses_1e3163ee6ffeIB93oV1sFojvZE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8b8fb23f3bd887a4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"__issue_context__.json"},"output":"<path>/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\nfibrochondrocyte\\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nmeniscus fibrochondrocyte - narrow synonym - PMID: [28939894](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28939894/)\\nFC - related synonym - abbreviation - PMID: [31871141](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31871141/)\\nfibrocartilage chondrocyte - exact synonym - PMID: 34608249\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nA chondrocyte with hybrid fibroblastic-chondrogenic characteristics found in fibrocartilage, particularly in the avascular inner zone and transitional middle zone of the meniscus (Wang et al., 2020).In humans, fibrochondrocytes are marked by predominant expression of type I collagen (COL1A1) and fibril-associated collagens (COL3A1, COL6A1) (Sun et al., 2019), while retaining type II collagen (COL2A1) expression and exhibiting lower SOX9 than hyaline chondrocytes (Liang et al., 2017).This molecular profile underlies the synthesis of abundant type I collagen essential for fibrocartilage matrix and reflects an intermediate phenotype between fibroblast and chondrocyte. \\n\\n**Parent cell type term** (check the hierarchy here https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl)\\n\\nConnective tissue cell \\nChondrocyte \\n\\n**Anatomical structure where the cell type is found** (check Uberon for anatomical structures: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/uberon)\\nPart of fibrocartilage\\n\\nexpresses some 'collagen alpha-1(I) chain'\\n\\n**Your ORCID**\\nhttps://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\\n\\n**Additional notes or concerns**\\n\\n\",\n3:   \"comments\": [],\n4:   \"title\": \"NTR - Fibrochondrocyte (FC)\",\n5:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3457\"\n6: }\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\nfibrochondrocyte\\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nmeniscus fibrochondrocyte - narrow synonym - PMID: [28939894](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28939894/)\\nFC - related synonym - abbreviation - PMID: [31871141](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31871141/)\\nfibrocartilage chondrocyte - exact synonym - PMID: 34608249\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nA chondrocyte with hybrid fibroblastic-chondrogenic characteristics found in fibrocartilage, particularly in the avascular inner zone and transitional middle zone of the meniscus (Wang et al., 2020).In humans, fibrochondrocytes are marked by predominant expression of type I collagen (COL1A1) and fibril-associated collagens (COL3A1, COL6A1) (Sun et al., 2019), while retaining type II collagen (COL2A1) expression and exhibiting lower SOX9 than hyaline chondrocytes (Liang et al., 2017).This molecular profile underlies the synthesis of abundant type I collagen essential for fibrocartilage matrix and reflects an intermediate phenotype between fibroblast and chondrocyte. \\n\\n**Parent cell type term** (check the hierarchy here https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl)\\n\\nConnective tissue cell \\nChondrocyte \\n\\n**Anatomical structure where the cell type is found** (check Uberon for anatomical structures: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/uberon)\\nPart of fibrocartilage\\n\\nexpresses some 'collagen alpha-1(I) c